 "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Rollback:** The most recent healthy release was v2.3.0. v2.3.1 (current) and v2.3.1-rc were both unhealthy, so I rolled back from v2.3.1 to v2.3.0. us-east, us-west and eu-west now all run v2.3.0, and the rollback reported as verified.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the health-check failures on v2.3.1 (about 18% error rate), the rollback to v2.3.0, and the follow-up work: confirm error-rate recovery and find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before re-releasing.\n\nI haven't re-checked the live health or error rate since the rollback, so confirming recovery is still open.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01JEowZ9wZtj74nszjpCitxR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01CjJnnrfgwy2znJ1Lo3eLXj", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent healthy release is v2.3.0. v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc are both unhealthy, so I'll roll back to v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_017KYQsdBRC76TdLw4whb2Xf", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.92}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_013fFQQXML9Ur9Yrd6Avshqp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy - rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 release (error rate ~18%, unhealthy in us-east, us-west, eu-west). v2.3.1-rc was also previously unhealthy. Action taken: rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release with healthy status, in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). Rollback reported VERIFIED with all regions on v2.3.0. Follow-up: confirm error rate recovery, investigate root cause of v2.3.1 failure before re-releasing.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-rollback-v2.3.0-2025", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Rollback:** The most recent healthy release was v2.3.0. v2.3.1 (current) and v2.3.1-rc were both unhealthy, so I rolled back from v2.3.1 to v2.3.0. us-east, us-west and eu-west now all run v2.3.0, and the rollback reported as verified.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the health-check failures on v2.3.1 (about 18% error rate), the rollback to v2.3.0, and the follow-up work: confirm error-rate recovery and find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before re-releasing.\n\nI haven't re-checked the live health or error rate since the rollback, so confirming recovery is still open.", "type": "text"}]}]}